<h4 id=3D"FUMCapability:BringYourOwnIdP(BYOI)-4.UserLifecycleManagement">4.=
 User Lifecycle Management</h4>
<h5 id=3D"FUMCapability:BringYourOwnIdP(BYOI)-a.Onboarding"><strong>a. Onbo=
arding</strong></h5>
<ol>
 <li><u>New user</u> - no compass profile, no NBC IDP profile<br><br>
  <ol>
   <li>Access profile - This setup and maintenance follows the current Comp=
ass FUM process of user management.<br><br></li>
   <li>Identity Profile - Identity profile for the new user will be created=
 automatically on NBC IDP and Compass.=20
    <ol>
     <li>This user configuration in Compass will be created with state=3Dac=
tive</li>
     <li>The user identity attributes will be populated based on user's id_=
token</li>
     <li>The identitySource attribute in the id_token will be recorded as a=
 user attribute. <br>
       External IDP integration will have idp value as neither nbin (reserv=
ed for NBC NBIN Okta tenant) nor nbc (reserved for NBC Employee Okta tenant=
) &nbsp;<br>
       These attributes will not be editable via Compass or NBC IDP and ded=
uced using the identitySource associated with the user.</li>
     <li>&nbsp;A default UG giving only wealth:access-control:viewer scope =
will be assigned to user on NBC IDP and Compass</li>
     <li>MFA - Client wants to disable MFA on NBC side&nbsp;<a class=3D"ext=
ernal-link" href=3D"https://support.okta.com/help/s/article/Exclude-from-OK=
ta-Verify-MFA-user-doesn-t-have-a-phone?language=3Den_US" rel=3D"nofollow" =
style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">https://support.okta.com/help/s/article/Ex=
clude-from-OKta-Verify-MFA-user-doesn-t-have-a-phone?language=3Den_US</a><s=
pan style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">&nbsp;<br>
        :warning: <span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">IAM architecture is verify=
ing the feasibility</span><br></span></li>
     <li>User attribute mapping=20
      <div class=3D"table-wrap">
       <table class=3D"wrapped confluenceTable">
        <colgroup>
         <col>
         <col>
         <col>
         <col>
         <col>
        </colgroup>
        <tbody>
         <tr>
          <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Attribute</th>
          <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Client IDP</th>
          <th class=3D"confluenceTh">NBC IDP</th>
          <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Compass</th>
          <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Description</th>
         </tr>
         <tr>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
           <p>First Name</p></td>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
           <p>(source)</p></td>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">(sync'd)</td>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
           <p>(sync'd)</p></td>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
           <p><br></p></td>
         </tr>
         <tr>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
           <p>Last Name</p></td>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
           <p>(source)</p></td>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">(sync'd)</td>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
           <p>(sync'd)</p></td>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
           <p><br></p></td>
         </tr>
         <tr>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
           <p>Unique User ID (Client Side)</p></td>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
           <p>(source)</p></td>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">bngfReferenceId (sync'd)</td>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
           <p>(sync'd)</p></td>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
           <p>unique user ID at Identity Source</p></td>
         </tr>
         <tr>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
           <p>Identity Source</p></td>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
           <p><br></p></td>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
           <p>(source)</p></td>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
           <p>(sync'd)</p></td>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
           <p>NBC provided 5 char unique string assigned to each client<br>
             assigned on NBC side based on integration configuration <br>
             with Client IDP</p></td>
         </tr>
         <tr>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
           <p>Login</p></td>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
           <p><br></p></td>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
           <p>(source)</p></td>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
           <p>(sync'd)</p></td>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
           <p><br></p></td>
         </tr>
         <tr>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
           <p>User ID</p></td>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
           <p><br></p></td>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
           <p>Okta ID (source)</p></td>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
           <p>(sync'd)</p></td>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
           <p><br></p></td>
         </tr>
         <tr>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
           <p>Subject</p></td>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
           <p><br></p></td>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
           <p>identitySource +&nbsp; '_' + bngfReferenceId (source)</p></td=
>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
           <p>(sync'd)</p></td>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
           <p><br></p></td>
         </tr>
         <tr>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
           <p>Language</p></td>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
           <p><br></p></td>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">(sync'd)</td>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
           <p>(sync'd)</p></td>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
           <p><br></p></td>
         </tr>
         <tr>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
           <p>Email</p></td>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
           <p>(source)</p></td>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">(sync'd)</td>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
           <p>(sync'd)</p></td>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
           <p><br></p></td>
         </tr>
         <tr>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Last Updated Date</td>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">(source)</td>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><br></td>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><br></td>
          <td class=3D"confluenceTd">date time of identity profile's last u=
pdate on client side&nbsp;</td>
         </tr>
        </tbody>
       </table>
      </div></li>
    </ol></li>
  </ol></li>
 <li><u style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">Migration</u><span style=3D"letter=
-spacing: 0.0px;"> - </span>Existing operational Compass profile.<br>
   &nbsp;=20
  <ol>
   <li>Case 1 - The existing user profile has username and idpSubject follo=
wing the standard (identitySource +&nbsp; '_' + uniqueClientUserId)<br>
     Okta=E2=80=99s account-linking will auto-connect this profile with Ext=
ernal SSO</li>
   <li>Case 2 - The existing user profile does <u>NOT</u> follow the standa=
rdized username and idpSubject<br>
    <ol>
     <li>Option 1 - Security Steward=20
      <ul>
       <li>A new access profile will be created cloned from the existing pr=
ofile <strong>ahead of first external sso login</strong>. <a href=3D"/space=
s/NBINDM/pages/2254868336/User+Configuration+API">User Configuration API</a=
> API # U1<br>
         The new profile will copy over <strong>only</strong> the access at=
tributes, overridden only by the values provided in the request.<br>
         This profile will generate username and idpSubject following the s=
tandard (identitySource +&nbsp; '_' + uniqueClientUserId)<br>
         The maintenance of access profile will follow the current Compass =
FUM process of user management.</li>
       <li>Upon first successful user login via external SSO, JIT provision=
ing will create an new identity profile in NBC IDP which will have the same=
 idpSubject and hence will link to this new cloned access profile.<span><br=
></span></li>
       <li><span><strong>If this clone isn't created ahead of first login</=
strong>, then the login will kick-off "new user" flow.</span>
        <ul>
         <li><span>The access profile for the new profile can still be copi=
ed over from the existing profile.&nbsp;</span><a href=3D"/spaces/NBINDM/pa=
ges/2254868336/User+Configuration+API">User Configuration API</a> API # U4<=
/li>
        </ul></li>
      </ul></li>
     <li><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">The existing profile will b=
e "decommissioned" by system (</span><a href=3D"/spaces/NA/pages/1230180707=
/User+Management#UserManagement-StateTransition">User Management#StateTrans=
ition</a><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">)</span></li>
     <li><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">Option 2 - Automated ( </sp=
an><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;"><strong>Conditional on acceptance by Clie=
nt and AAA</strong></span> )=20
      <ul>
       <li>The existing profile will be associated with a link-code as a sy=
stem generated UUID by the security steward.</li>
       <li>This link-code will be provided to the client by NBIN operations=
 and would need to be added as an attribute to the user on the Client IDP.<=
/li>
       <li>Upon the first external SSO, a new identity profile will be crea=
ted and associated with a cloned access profile using link-code as user att=
ribute which was passed during the login.<br><span class=3D"confluence-embe=
dded-file-wrapper confluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence=
-embedded-image" draggable=3D"false" height=3D"334" src=3D"0892bb9afa5ea487=
39e2c9a1676d68c92078c3783b78017dbdde5e2afad21f6f" data-image-src=3D"/downlo=
ad/attachments/1678277031/image-2024-4-17_11-16-0.png?version=3D1&amp;modif=
icationDate=3D1713366960343&amp;api=3Dv2" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"=
0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"1817442156" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1=
" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment" data-linked-resource-default-ali=
as=3D"image-2024-4-17_11-16-0.png" data-base-url=3D"https://wiki.bnc.ca" da=
ta-linked-resource-content-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-containe=
r-id=3D"1678277031" data-linked-resource-container-version=3D"78" tabindex=
=3D"0" alt=3D"" width=3D"468"></span></li>
      </ul></li>
    </ol></li>
   <li>Compass R2 login de-activation</li>
  </ol></li>
</ol>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 80.0px;">Current FUM process passes an activation =
date (Compass X) to Compass R2, which indicates the date on which the R2 pr=
ofile should be de-activated. API Ref # U1 and U4.<br>
  Association of R2 profile on Compass FUM activates the above flow.<br>
  User access profiles for external SSO will be created new, cloned from an=
 existing profile or updated.<br>
  Hence, these endpoints will also trigger the flow to pass the activation =
date to R2 using the existing FUM architecture.<br>
  If an activation date already exists in Compass R2, it is required to upd=
ate the activation date to the higher of the two values and store the addit=
ional compass idp (new / cloned).&nbsp;<br>
  :warning: <span style=3D"color:#09326c;"><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">F=
UM architecture to confirm this approach.</span></span></p>
<h5 id=3D"FUMCapability:BringYourOwnIdP(BYOI)-b.Update"><strong>b. Update</=
strong></h5>
<ol>
 <li>Identity attributes<br>
  <p>User identity attributes will be checked for update on each login. See=
 SSO flow (above) for details<br><br></p></li>
 <li>Access profile attributes=20
  <ol>
   <li>Compass authorization<br>
     User authorization will be maintained in Compass as per existing FUM p=
rocess<br><br></li>
   <li>System integration=20
    <ol>
     <li>Compass R2 - Update to R2 ID (if permitted in FUM) needs to be sen=
d to Compass R2 as per the current Compass-X and R2 integration architectur=
e.</li>
     <li>Secure Zone<br>
       The secure zone ID is currently stored in NBC Okta and will be repla=
ced by SZ's identity cross-reference (ICR) API along with an Okta hook to e=
nsure SZ ID remain part of the access token issued by Okta.<br>
       As of now, NBIN user population isn't onboarded onto ICR and hence, =
Compass X needs to continue to store the SZ ID and allow an Okta hook integ=
ration to ensure SZ ID are part of the access token but not managed on Okta=
.<br><span style=3D"color:#09326c;"><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">:warning=
: FUM and IAM architecture to confirm this approach</span></span></li>
    </ol></li>
  </ol></li>
</ol>
<h5 id=3D"FUMCapability:BringYourOwnIdP(BYOI)-c.Off-boarding"><strong>c. Of=
f-boarding</strong></h5>
<p><strong><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper confluence-embed=
ded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image confluence-thumbna=
il" draggable=3D"false" height=3D"397" src=3D"1439aa31f43b5c21b59c7c5dd317d=
37e7db8775796ae14d820a5c5b81b2a387e" data-image-src=3D"/download/attachment=
s/1678277031/image-2024-3-27_15-2-36.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=
=3D1711566156677&amp;api=3Dv2" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-lin=
ked-resource-id=3D"1800756987" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-link=
ed-resource-type=3D"attachment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"image=
-2024-3-27_15-2-36.png" data-base-url=3D"https://wiki.bnc.ca" data-linked-r=
esource-content-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"167=
8277031" data-linked-resource-container-version=3D"78" tabindex=3D"0" alt=
=3D"" width=3D"468"></span></strong></p>
<p>i. Based on inactivity</p>
<p>There will be a time-based profile deletion for users with no activity</=
p>
<ul>
 <li>After an initial period of inactivity (initial_inactivity_days in FUM =
firm configuration) the user profile on NBC Okta will be deleted. <br>
   If the user logs in after this period, the NBC Okta profile will get aut=
o-created again.</li>
 <li>After an extended period of inactivity, (where the user profile on Ext=
ernal IDP is deleted) Compass will suspend the profile.</li>
 <li>After an NBC default period of not being re-instated, the user profile=
 will be deleted in Compass.</li>
</ul>
<p>ii. User leaving the Client Firm</p>
<ul>
 <li>If a user leaves a client firm, Compass can put the user profile direc=
tly in a suspended state.</li>
</ul>
<h4 id=3D"FUMCapability:BringYourOwnIdP(BYOI)-FUMenhancement"><span style=
=3D"color:#0055cc;"><strong>FUM enhancement</strong></span></h4>
<p><strong>Firm Configuration / Management</strong></p>
<ol>
 <li>Add column for firm specific content API message key (cx-access-unset-=
key) for users that don't have Authorization setup in Compass yet</li>
 <li>Add column for firm specific userLogoutUrl</li>
 <li>Add column for idp (the identitySource configured in Okta). Configure =
these values as part of Compass firm onboarding. This value must be a 6 dig=
it fixed length unique string.</li>
 <li>Update FM1 and FM2 to support the 3 fields above. <a href=3D"/spaces/N=
BINDM/pages/2254868366/Firm+Management+API">Firm Management API</a></li>
 <li>Update FM3 to return these 3 fields</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>User Configuration</strong></p>
<ol>
 <li>Create following fields in user configuration table=20
  <ol>
   <li>bngfReferenceId - unique user ID assigned and maintained by client f=
irm (if any) or a nbin generated unique value.</li>
   <li>sourceIdpSub (optional)</li>
   <li>'identity_last_updated' - datetime, This field will be updated for "=
all" users (across IDPs) but only when their identity attributes are update=
d.</li>
   <li>'accessProfileSet' - boolean, This field is true when the user's acc=
ess profile is defined.<br><a href=3D"/spaces/NBINDM/pages/2254868336/User+=
Configuration+API">User Configuration API</a><br>
     This attribute will be <strong>set</strong> upon the successful execut=
ion (or equivalent) of API # UF2 (feature-package) and U1, U4 if a feature-=
package is assigned<br>
     This attribute will be <strong>unset</strong> upon the successful exec=
ution (or equivalent) of API # UF3 (feature-package)</li>
  </ol></li>
 <li>Create two numeric fields in firm configuration=20
  <ol>
   <li>initial_inactivity_days (NBC default unless customized by firm)</li>
   <li>extended_inactivity_days (NBC default unless customized by firm)</li=
>
  </ol></li>
 <li>Create endpoint U11 as described on <a href=3D"/spaces/NBINDM/pages/22=
54868336/User+Configuration+API">User Configuration API</a></li>
 <li>Update U2 to return firm_id or 404 when user not found.</li>
 <li>Update U1 to always create user name with the scheme: identitySource +=
&nbsp; '_' + bngfReferenceId. Ref point #1</li>
 <li>Update U1 and U4 to=20
  <ol>
   <li>allow activation date in the request header and send the same to R2<=
/li>
   <li>push updates to Okta for attributes like language <u>only</u> when i=
dp =3D nbin</li>
   <li>allow updates to identity/personal profile attributes&nbsp;<u>only</=
u> when idp =3D nbin</li>
   <li>send event message to R2, updating about the R2 activation date</li>
  </ol></li>
 <li>UF9, UF10 and UF11 to be allowed <u>only</u> when idp =3D nbin&nbsp;</=
li>
 <li>UF11,&nbsp;<span style=3D"color:#000000;">If the user profile has sour=
ceIdp then call UF13 for it, using system_token.</span></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Compass UI</strong></p>
<ol>
 <li><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;">Feature - Manage User Profile Details =
=3D Ability to update users personal profile details</span></li>
 <li><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;">Feature - Admin User Profile =3D Abilit=
y to manage profile actions, reset password, 2FA etc</span></li>
 <li>User Status to be displayed by combining the user status and accessPro=
fileSet (user profile attribute). Ref <span style=3D"color:#000000;"><a hre=
f=3D"/spaces/NWPI/pages/1805139524/Firm+SSO+-+Experience+Design">Firm SSO -=
 Experience Design</a></span></li>
</ol>
<h4 id=3D"FUMCapability:BringYourOwnIdP(BYOI)-CompassUXsupport"><span style=
=3D"color:#0055cc;">Compass UX support</span></h4>
<ol>
 <li style=3D"color:#000000;"><span style=3D"color:#000000;">User Configura=
tion</span>
  <ol>
   <li style=3D"color:#000000;"><span style=3D"color:#000000;">identity_las=
t_updated - date time for identity update</span></li>
   <li style=3D"color:#000000;"><span style=3D"color:#000000;">accessProfil=
eSet - status of access profile being set/unset</span></li>
   <li style=3D"color:#000000;"><span style=3D"color:#000000;">state transi=
tion - This hasn't been affected and hence the status continues to be the s=
ame and agnostic to the identitySource of a user.</span></li>
   <li>bngfReferenceId - unique user ID assigned and maintained by client f=
irm (if any) or a nbin generated unique value.</li>
   <li style=3D"color:#000000;"><span style=3D"color:#000000;">idp - repres=
ents the identitySource of the user</span>
    <ol>
     <li style=3D"color:#000000;"><span style=3D"color:#000000;">nbc - empl=
oyee</span></li>
     <li style=3D"color:#000000;"><span style=3D"color:#000000;">nbin - nbi=
n user with identity maintained in NBC IDP</span></li>
     <li style=3D"color:#000000;"><span style=3D"color:#000000;"><em>&lt;an=
y other value&gt;</em> - nbin user with identity managed on their firm's ID=
P</span></li>
    </ol></li>
  </ol></li>
 <li><span style=3D"color:#000000;"><a href=3D"/spaces/NWPI/pages/180513952=
4/Firm+SSO+-+Experience+Design">Firm SSO - Experience Design</a></span></li=
>
</ol>
<h1 id=3D"FUMCapability:BringYourOwnIdP(BYOI)-References">References</h1>
<ol>
 <li><a href=3D"/spaces/NA/pages/1230180707/User+Management#UserManagement-=
StateTransition">User Management#StateTransition</a></li>
</ol>
<h2 id=3D"FUMCapability:BringYourOwnIdP(BYOI)-6.2Phase-2:OnboardClientFirm=
=E2=80=99sSecurityStewards">6.2 Phase - 2:&nbsp;Onboard Client Firm=E2=80=
=99s Security Stewards</h2>
<p>Allow limited access for External Security Stewards to assign pre-define=
d roles to their own users</p>
<h3 id=3D"FUMCapability:BringYourOwnIdP(BYOI)-6.2.1Objectives"><strong>6.2.=
1 Objectives</strong></h3>
<h3 id=3D"FUMCapability:BringYourOwnIdP(BYOI)-6.2.2Strategy"><strong>6.2.2 =
Strategy</strong></h3>
<h3 id=3D"FUMCapability:BringYourOwnIdP(BYOI)-6.2.3Solution"><strong>6.2.3 =
Solution</strong></h3>
<p><strong>1.&nbsp;User Configuration</strong></p>
<p>A new role =E2=80=98manager=E2=80=99 will be created for User Configurat=
ion. The endpoints governed by this role will User identity attributes will=
 be checked for update on each login</p>
<p><br></p>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
